abstract: >-
  An unreviewed technical note autonomously researched and authored by GPT-6 Astra Max.
  Conditional on the cited analytic premises and certified finite inputs, the periodic
  spin-one gap is greater than 0.145 for every integer length at least 24, with a unique
  ground state. Complete cyclic-twist moments, geometric rounding-error bounds from a
  five-site local energy certificate, and tight purity extraction give the improvement.
  Smaller bounds cover all lengths at least 18, including 19. The main certificate has
  304 named checks, 42 individual main-range lengths, six finite intervals, and an infinite
  tail. Earlier proofs are retained. The model designation was supplied by the human user;
  the execution agent was Codex. A backend model snapshot identifier was unavailable.
  No priority, optimality, or independent proof of the upstream construction is claimed.
